      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Marasini et al.",
        "AbstractText": "The whole-genome sequence of Bacillus velezensis strain SB1216, isolated from the Great Salt Plains of Oklahoma, showed the presence of a 3,814,720-bp circular chromosome and no plasmids. The presence of a novel 870-bp extracellular RNase gene is predicted to be responsible for this strain's antitumor activity."
